          "path": "_m/g/f/h/0/mccaig-s-tower-wp/12-09-08-mccaig-s-tower-oban-7.jpg",
          "filename": "12.09.08 McCaig's Tower, Oban (7372839368).jpg",
          "caption": "Looking across the waterfront at Oban, seen here is McCaig's Tower sitting on Battery Hill. Commissioned by John Stuart McCaig and completed in 1902, the monument is there to provide a lasting memory to his family. Styled on the Colosseum in Rome, his plans were to build a museum and art gallery along with a central tower. However he died before his project was completed and thus the folly remains with only the outer walls.",
          "alt": "Looking across the waterfront at Oban, seen here is McCaig's Tower sitting on Battery Hill. Commissioned by John Stuart McCaig and completed in 1902, the monument is there to provide a lasting memory to his family. Styled on the Colosseum in Rome, his plans were to build a museum and art gallery along with a central tower. However he died before his project was completed and thus the folly remains with only the outer walls.",
          "width": 2816,
          "height": 2112,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
